Project 03 – Personal Expense Tracker with CSV

I developed a Personal Expense Tracker using Python.

The application allows users to add, view and filter expenses by category and month. It stores expense records in a CSV file so that the information remains available after restarting the program.

It also calculates category-wise spending, the grand total and the biggest individual expense.

Problem fixed: I handled invalid date formats and negative or non-numeric expense amounts using input validation.

Python concepts used: Functions, loops, dictionaries, CSV file handling, datetime validation and exception handling.
